# Rust
/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# cargo-mutants scratch output. It lands in the repo root by default; pass
# `--output <dir>` outside the tree when running a mutation pass, and this is the
# backstop for when that is forgotten.
mutants.out/

# Node / web client tooling
node_modules/
dist/
out/

# Python bytecode from the scripts under tools/. `tools/portability-census.py` leaves
# `tools/__pycache__/` behind on every run, and nothing covered it — so the tree was dirty
# on this machine and would be dirty in any clone that ran the script.
__pycache__/

# Built multi-page sites (taliesin build <dir> default output)
_site/
_book/

# Persistent execution cache (rendered cell outputs, keyed by cumulative content
# hash); regenerated on demand, like the build output above.
_freeze/

# Single-file `taliesin build <file>` output (and the extension resources it copies)
# that lands beside its source — the `_site/`/`_book/` rules above only cover the
# directory build. These are regenerable artifacts, not source; the `.tmd` and the
# tracked `_extensions/` copies are the sources of truth.
corpus/liquid-glass-slides/example.html
corpus/liquid-glass-slides/liquid-glass.js
crates/core/tests/fixtures/deck-ext/slides.html

# Media generated by code cells beside their own document: a cell writing audio
# (`scipy.io.wavfile`), or a `#| fig-export:` / `ggsave` figure. Cells now run in
# the document's directory, so these land next to the source; they regenerate on
# render, so they're ignored rather than committed. The deliberate `.wav` fixtures
# under corpus/tech-blog/ are already tracked and unaffected (git keeps tracked
# files regardless of these rules). `/*.wav` stays as a backstop for the old
# repo-root dump from before cells ran in the document's directory.
/*.wav
corpus/posts/fourier-transform/*.wav
**/figures/

# Logs and env
*.log
.env
.env.local

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.swp

# Per-machine agent settings. These carry absolute local paths and a personal
# permission allowlist, so they must never be committed. Until 2026-08-03 only the
# AUTHOR'S MACHINE-GLOBAL ignore (~/.config/git/ignore) covered this, which is
# invisible in a clone: `corpus/tech-blog/.claude/settings.local.json` was one
# `git add -f` — or one fresh clone on another machine — away from being published.
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# subagent-driven-development scratch
.superpowers/

# NOTE: tools/live-edit-bench/RESULTS.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It was, until
# 2026-08-02, and that is why a 10x payload regression on 2026-06-30 sat unnoticed for
# five weeks while RESULTS.md kept publishing the pre-regression headline. Committing it
# makes a regeneration show up as a reviewable diff. The three *_ns timing fields drift
# per run; the structural fields do not, and regression.rs gates them.

# ad-hoc Python kernel venv for local audits
.venv-audit/

# the kernel venv the interpreter resolver finds on its own: step 2 (<project>/.venv)
# and step 4 (ancestor .venv, which walks up to this repo root and stops at .git), so
# one venv here serves every corpus document with no TALIESIN_PYTHON to remember.
.venv/

# Leftover scratch output from the deleted `tools/ui-audit` harness (340 MB of
# generated pages). The directory carried its own .gitignore until that harness was
# removed on 2026-08-13; deleting it un-ignored the tree.
.work/
